{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446651-with-v5-is-there-a-possibility-to-put-one-tremere-house-against-another","id":1446651,"title":"With V5 is there a possibility to put one tremere house against another?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T13:33:40-07:00","id":1446651,"title":"With V5 is there a possibility to put one tremere house against another?","content":"So im a playing a Nosferatu that is interested in fucking the Tremere over, and now that they took a heavy blow and their clan is basically fragmented, i think theres a good opportunity, but which house should i &quot;&quot;&quot;support&quot;&quot;&quot; which one of them would be the easiest to pick one by one after they dealt with other tremere? also i know Tremere have a lot of enemies but who would be most interested in their demise?<br /> and how could i go about this plan,to ensure i survive this, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T13:42:54-07:00","id":1446653,"title":"","content":"Support either Karna or Ipssissimus. For different reasons.<br /> <br /> The Banu Hagim are always a good group to support if you are trying to wear down the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T13:50:32-07:00","id":1446655,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.redd.it/tki17gy9uoa41.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Alas, I do not know enough of the nitty-gritty about the new Tremere factions to have a strong suggestion for which one to back if your ultimate goal is to destroy the Tremere Clan. Either the &quot;core&quot; Clan behind Shrekt or House Goratrix in the Sabbat (quite possibly being run by Tremere him(it?)self in a new body) would likely try to consolidate rather than obliterate, and the smaller factions like Carna and Ipsissimus(?) probably aren't going to be interested in picking fights generally.<br /> <br /> Regarding other enemies to pick from, oh there is a list.<ul><li> Tzimisce</li> <li> Sabbat Warrior Salubri</li> <li> Pretty much any branch of the Banu Haqim, to varying extents</li> <li> Vengeful Gargoyles, and their &quot;relatives&quot; among the Nosferatu and Gangrel</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Probably others I am forgetting. The Sabbat is probably the best faction to go to looking for weapons against the Tremere. The Tzimisce despise them, as do the Warrior Salubri for obvious reasons. I'm of two minds about the Banu Haqim antitribu; on the one hand, they skipped out on the Curse so don't necessarily have reason to resent that, but maybe resent being forced to split with their brethren over the matter, dunno. I don't know enough about the Gargoyles to know how many of them are especially resentful towards the Tremere, but I've read a bit of source material that hints some members of Clans Gangrel and Nosferatu are just waiting for a chance to wreck the Tremere for what they pulled.<br /> <br /> And oh look the &quot;majority&quot; of the Gangrel Clan is no longer even nominally a member of the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:24:36-07:00","id":1446785,"title":"","content":"I think its very likely that all the different houses are a front and the split was a public relations move so that they could spread the tremere out and not all be targeted by a long list of enemies. Siding with one against the other is a good way to get sold out. <br /> <br /> Ignoring that,The real issue is how much do you want to gain, how much you want to destroy, and how much you want to live to the end of it? <br /> <br /> second issue is geography. Most likely there's only going to be one kind of Tremere in your locality. Maybe two. Very unlikely to be 3 and near impossible 4. <br /> <br /> Maximum Gains? Side-with or target Ippsimus or Goratrix. (but maybe just ask some Nos elders)<br /> Max damage? Well you'll want to target the OG tremere. <br /> Maximum survivability? look at your st's preferences. The OG's should logically be better at magic, but have a lot of enemies. conversly House Carna should be bad at magic, but maybe they've struck a chord with your ST and they are destined to be the last Magi standing with their shortcomings sidelined due to biases. <br /> <br /> Honestly, Magic sucks in this edition. If you want to war woth the tremere for magic you might as well join a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-07-2021, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T08:45:37-07:00","id":1446796,"title":"","content":"Sell them out to the local mages...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T09:07:53-07:00","id":1446798,"title":"","content":"Maybe House Tremere, because they're closest to the Tremere responsible for the various tribal grudges; Houses Carna and Ipssissimus haven't really done anything yet. Goratrix are implied to have the most heinous practices, which could make them easier to ostracise, but we haven't been told a lot about their status so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:36:20-07:00","id":1446839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446651-with-v5-is-there-a-possibility-to-put-one-tremere-house-against-another?p=1446798#post1446798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe House Tremere, because they're closest to the Tremere responsible for the various tribal grudges; Houses Carna and Ipssissimus haven't really done anything yet. Goratrix are implied to have the most heinous practices, which could make them easier to ostracise, but we haven't been told a lot about their status so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Part of the issue with House Goratrix in play - as i see it at least - is what kind of person Goratrix/Tremere actually is and how much of a hand each of them had in the Tremere antitribu for their 4-5 centuries of existence, among other things (like how aware are other kindred of the possibility of Goratrix actually being possessed by Tremere for decades or centuries, depending on which version of the canon one is using).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:48:24-07:00","id":1447063,"title":"","content":"I would say the likeliest is the Cam Tremere Houses against House Impsissimus. Because from the few parts I have on them in the Anarch book they are willing to go far and deep for magical knowledge like &quot;Progress justify any mean&quot; and they are heavyly against any of the three because in their eyes only try to brainwash people to be loyal mindslaves again.<br /> It is said that there is a &quot;fight&quot; for Vienna too.<br /> But honestly the whole Tremere story seems in V5 to me that they want to make it clear, that the three cam houses are not evil (anymore) and the anarchs are bad because they are rioters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}